{
  "schema": "semio.quiz.home-grid/v1",
  "description": "The overview of a quiz site: cards over a glass layer, the real page of each card on the strip behind it. Pages in reading order (DOM, focus and visual order at every width): learner, quiz 1, introduction, quiz 2, leaderboard, quiz 3, badges, quiz 4, preferences; quizzes a catalog lacks leave no gap, quizzes beyond the fourth follow the preferences. Each page's strip cell is where its card sits: row by row in three columns on desktop, in two columns on tablets with the leaderboard on a row of its own. At rest the overview is a live grid of every page and the card layer shares its tracks, each card in its page's cell; by viewport width at the design system's breakpoints: a list of sections in one column up to the mobile maximum, two equal columns over five equal rows up to the tablet maximum (the leaderboard alone on its row), three columns weighted 1 : 1.5 : 1 over three rows weighted 1 : 1.4 : 1 from there (the leaderboard in the larger centre cell). The leaderboard card shows the first five rows by rank and the own row apart when it ranks lower.",
